1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Container With Most Water — LeetCode 11

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,200
Problem: each bar is a vertical line. Pick two so they hold the most water between them.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:10,200
The area is min of the two heights, times the distance between them.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:14,000
Key idea: start as wide as possible — one line at each end.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,500
Water is capped by the SHORTER line, so moving the taller one only loses width.

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,500
Always move the shorter line inward — it's the only move that could ever help.

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,500
Widest first: min(1,7) × 8 = 8. The left line is shortest, so l moves in.

8
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Now min(8,7) × 7 = 49 — a big jump. That becomes our max.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Keep moving the shorter side. Every other pair is narrower and never beats 49.

10
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,500
The winner is lines 1 and 8: min(8,7) × 7 = 49.

11
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:44,000
Moving the shorter line is safe because the taller one can't raise a shrinking container.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
One pass from both ends: O(n) time, O(1) space.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,500
